    "summary": "Iran's supreme leader appointed Mohsen Rezaei, a longtime Revolutionary Guards (IRGC) commander, as secretary of Iran's Supreme National Security Council on August 9-10, 2026, replacing Mohammad Zolghadr. Rezaei was also designated as the supreme leader's representative to the SNSC. The same day, the supreme leader appointed six senior military commanders across the Armed Forces, IRGC, and Basij in what was described as a major military leadership reshuffle. The appointments formalized parts of a wartime leadership structure. The supreme leader also ordered the integration of the Armed Forces General Staff with the Khatam al-Anbiya Central Headquarters, the joint operational command. These moves were characterized as a consolidation of power and hardline orientation, establishing war commanders in influential roles during a period when Iran faced significant security challenges.",
